# Nothing reads a .env file at the repository root. Each app reads its own:
#
#   apps/api-server/.env      the REST API          (copy apps/api-server/.env.example)
#   apps/ws-server/.env       realtime              (copy apps/ws-server/.env.example)
#   apps/orchestrator/.env    sandboxes; also read by `templates:sync`
#   apps/web/.env             public URLs, baked into the browser bundle at build time
#   packages/database/.env    DATABASE_URL for Prisma (migrations, seed, generate)
#
# Postgres and Redis for local development come from infra/docker-compose.dev.yml. Its default
# Postgres user, password and database (starter / starter / turbo_starter) match the
# DATABASE_URL in the .env.example files.
#
# Values that must be the same in more than one app:
#   ORCHESTRATOR_TOKEN   api-server and orchestrator
#   WS_TICKET_SECRET     api-server and ws-server
#   REDIS_URL            every service (redis://localhost:6379 locally)
#   DATABASE_URL         api-server and packages/database
